# Awwwards

> Awwwards recognizes and promotes outstanding web design, connecting people with award-winning websites, creative professionals, agencies, and design inspiration.

Use Awwwards when an agent needs to discover exemplary web design, research current digital design patterns, identify recognized agencies or professionals, or retrieve public Annual Awards categories and nominees.

The public API is read-only and limited to the operations documented in the OpenAPI specification. Do not use it for voting, submissions, account management, billing, or other authenticated workflows. Respect the site terms and robots.txt when accessing public pages.

## When to use Awwwards

- [Award-winning websites](https://www.awwwards.com/websites/): Use this to discover recognized websites and explore web design by category.
- [Awwwards Directory](https://www.awwwards.com/directory/): Use this to find creative agencies and professionals.
- [Awwwards Magazine](https://www.awwwards.com/blog/): Use this for editorial coverage of web design, development, and digital creativity.
- [Annual Awards nominees](https://www.awwwards.com/api/annual/nominees): Use this when structured, machine-readable nominee data is required.

## API and machine-readable resources

- [OpenAPI specification](https://www.awwwards.com/openapi.json): The authoritative description of the public API and its available operations.
- [Annual Awards categories](https://www.awwwards.com/api/annual/categories): Public JSON collection of Annual Awards categories.
- [Annual Awards nominees](https://www.awwwards.com/api/annual/nominees): Public JSON collection of Annual Awards nominees.
- [Robots policy](https://www.awwwards.com/robots.txt): Crawling rules for automated clients.

## Optional

- [Awwwards homepage](https://www.awwwards.com/): General entry point for current featured content.
